{
  "id": "COMPOUND:18030 - PROTEIN:5781",
  "verbalization": "Ustusol A is implicated in the regulation of A2780cisR through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Ustusol A acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One and Cocosamide B, which in turn target A2780cisR. This indicates a potential pathway where Ustusol A may influence the activity of these compounds, which then exert their effects on A2780cisR. The presence of multiple targets and the shared involvement of 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One in linking Ustusol A to A2780cisR suggests a possible mechanism involving the modulation of signaling pathways or enzymatic activities. The integration of these relationships highlights the complexity of the interaction network, emphasizing the role of Ustusol A as a central node in this regulatory cascade.",
